<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Gujarat Sultanate</h1><p class="st-meta">1407 CE – 1573 CE · capital Ahmedabad</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A rich maritime sultanate of western India that built Ahmedabad and fought the Portuguese for control of the Arabian Sea.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muzaffar-shah-i">Zafar Khan</a>, governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tughlaq-dynasty">Tughluqs</a>, declared independence in 1407 as Muzaffar Shah after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur's</a> sack of Delhi left the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> powerless. His grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-shah-i-of-gujarat">Ahmad Shah I</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmedabad">Ahmedabad</a> in 1411 on the Sabarmati river and made it the capital of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/muzaffarid-dynasty">Muzaffarid dynasty</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat's</a> ports, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khambhat">Cambay</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/surat">Surat</a> and Diu, were hubs of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean-trade">Indian Ocean trade</a> in textiles, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indigo">indigo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spice-trade">spices</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-begada">Mahmud Begada</a>, the greatest sultan, captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/champaner">Champaner</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/junagadh-state">Junagadh</a>, and his fleet with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluks</a> fought the Portuguese at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaul">Chaul</a> and Diu. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmedabad">Ahmedabad's</a> mosques, with their carved stone screens such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sidi-saiyyed-mosque">Sidi Saiyyed</a>, blend Islamic and local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> and Jain craftsmanship.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahadur-shah-of-gujarat">Bahadur Shah</a> ceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasai">Bassein</a> and allowed a fort at Diu to the Portuguese and was killed by them in 1537. Weak successors and noble factions followed, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a> conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> in 1572 to 1573.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/gujarat-sultanate.jpg" alt="Gujarat Sultanate" width="320" height="297"><figcaption>Image: Beylarbey · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Political_boundary_of_the_Gujarat_Sultanate_in_1490.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1407 CE – 1573 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ahmedabad</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ahmad Shah I, Mahmud Begada, Bahadur Shah</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Persian, Gujarati</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Muzaffarid dynasty, Sultanate of Gujarat</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1490&amp;focus=gujarat-sultanate" aria-label="Gujarat Sultanate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6619 1328 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Gujarat Sultanate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6939 1584L7048 1646M6939 1584L7018 1385M6939 1584L7018 1385M6939 1584L7019 1609"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7048 1646h0M7018 1385h0M7018 1385h0M7019 1609h0"/><path class="map-